  "question": {
    "text": "The transition from the state $n=4$ to $n=3$ in a hydrogen like atom results in ultraviolet radiation. Infrared radiation will be obtained in the transition from",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2XDAj",
      "text": "\n$2 \\rightarrow 1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "x8QZ3",
      "text": "\n$3 \\rightarrow 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Wo63d",
      "text": "\n$4 \\rightarrow 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "66wjL",
      "text": "\n$5 \\rightarrow 4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "IR corresponds to least value of $\\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2}-\\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$\ni.e. from Paschen, Bracket and Pfund series. Thus the transition corresponds to $5 \\rightarrow 3$.",
    "image": null
  },
